# After changing the mod: commit, then deploy

Both steps, every time, unless told otherwise.

1. Commit and push to `origin/main`.
2. Copy the deployment set into the local game so the change can be tested.

The deployment set is exactly what the game loads, and matches what
`publish.yml` packs: `metadata.lua`, `items.lua`, `Code/`, `Images/`. Never copy
docs, `templates/`, `tools/` or `.github/`.

```powershell
$src  = "D:\PROJS\SMR\smr-community-fixes"
$dest = "$env:APPDATA\Surviving Mars Relaunched\Mods\smr-community-fixes"
robocopy "$src\Code"   "$dest\Code"   /MIR /NFL /NDL /NJH /NJS /NP
robocopy "$src\Images" "$dest\Images" /MIR /NFL /NDL /NJH /NJS /NP
Copy-Item "$src\metadata.lua","$src\items.lua" -Destination $dest -Force
$global:LASTEXITCODE = 0   # robocopy returns 1 on success
```

`/MIR` deletes anything in the destination that is not in the source, so keep it
pointed at those two subfolders and never at the Mods root.

## Never touch another mod

`%APPDATA%\Surviving Mars Relaunched\Mods\` holds many unrelated mods. Only
`smr-community-fixes` may be written to. Read another mod's files when
diagnosing something — a callstack often points into one — but never modify,
move, disable or delete them.

## Reading game output

Logs are in `%APPDATA%\Surviving Mars Relaunched\logs`, newest last. The build
is `MarsDebug.exe`, so engine asserts appear with a Lua callstack naming the mod
and file responsible — check which mod it actually names before assuming it is
this one.
